component SigilImplementationClaims {
  goal {
    Present whole code files for independent claims readings against the design
    names inside configured promise scope, and judge the implementation against
    those promises after the full design check.
  }

  interface {
    CodeVocabulary {
      Describe code elements, actions and measures in their own vocabulary.
      Separate observations from interpreter-written realizes mappings.
      Component realization establishes membership; Tag realization states delivery.
      A test element's mappings account for its exercise of the design and never
      establish implementation membership or delivery.
    }

    CodeGuidance {
      Publish compiled code guidance under its own fingerprint and vocabulary
      generation. Extract copies only outside the workspace under validation.
      Teach unmapped elements as faithful readings of undesigned code.
    }

    FileRequests {
      Present each selected whole file in a safe directory carrying full source,
      qualified design names, admitted design claims, exact Facet context and code
      guidance. Bind each request to its path, content, names, effective selection,
      code guidance and vocabulary generation. List empty files, skipped symlinks,
      automatic design exclusions and unpresentable files separately.
    }

    AlignCommands {
      Offer align prepare, align ingest and align check in the single sigilc executable. Read selection from
      workspace configuration, refuse nonempty output directories, and launch no
      interpreter. Present only files with stale or unread readings, and report reuse.
      Ingest one file against its own binding; name every field that changed.
      Accept either binding or rows from standard input, never both at once.
    }

    ImplementationLaws {
      Judge only scoped design commitments against independent production code
      observations. Component membership and Tag delivery answer provides;
      dependencies on components or their Tags can answer requires through a
      delivering service. Enforce exclusions, required state owners, exclusive
      ownership and latency or calendar-day budgets. Keep unmapped writers visible
      and count multiple members of one rightful component as one owner.
      Test elements never establish production membership, delivery or ownership.
      Logic, Cases and negative claims can breach but never demand an answer.
    }

    AlignCheck {
      Gate the implementation laws on the complete linked design, including
      sources outside configured promise roots. An incomplete or disjoint design,
      unread code or an unpresentable file makes alignment Incomplete. Otherwise
      disagreements, undesigned files or elements, and unanswered required promises
      make Drift. Clean coherent design is Closed; clean loose design is Converged.
      Closed and Converged exit zero, Drift and Incomplete exit one, usage exits
      two and operational failure exits three. No command launches an interpreter.
    }

    LocatedFindings {
      Write the versioned workspace report and judgment context under claims.
      Each finding names its law, design claims and Facet spans, and code rows
      with whole-file locations. Locations use UTF-8 byte offsets and a SHA256
      digest of captured source bytes. Report incomplete reasons, unread files,
      undesigned code, unanswered promises, active exclusion counts, components
      outside promise scope and identity digests.
    }

    FileReadings {
      Admit data-only code rows against the file's presented names. Resolve
      qualified labels and unique bare labels to design identities. Refuse only
      this file on a defect; empty or elementless answers keep it unread.
      Store local element names under claims/implementation using content, code
      guidance and vocabulary identities, so a path rename reuses the reading.
      Ask again for changed code, changed cited names, changed component membership
      promises, or newly added names when elements remain undesigned. Unrelated
      design edits leave the reading fresh. An identical ingest makes no write.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    CodeVocabulary {
      The unit of code is the whole file. No language parser or source annotation
      supplies an implementation mapping. File location alone is no membership
      evidence. An unmapped element must remain visible.
    }

    FileReadings {
      Rules and nested expressions refuse the whole answer. An action target is
      a presented design name, never another file's element. Each referenced
      element must be declared within this file. Ambiguous labels list qualified
      alternatives, and every mapping originates in the interpreter's rows.
    }
  }
}
